# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules. The hashed JS/CSS bundles
# already have unique filenames per build (content-addressed), so they're
# safe to cache forever -- but the top-level HTML pages (/, /app,
# /architecture, etc.) share the same URL across deploys, so without an
# explicit rule an edge cache or a visitor's browser can keep serving an
# old build's HTML after a new one ships.
#
# The /* block also carries the site-wide security response headers. The
# Content-Security-Policy is NOT written here -- scripts/build-csp.mjs appends
# it to dist/_headers at the end of `npm run build`, because four pages ship an
# inline <script> (app.html's theme switch, coming-soon's calculator, and the
# waitlist forms on /community and /challenge) and the policy has to carry a
# sha256 of each. Hand-maintained hashes go stale the first time one of those
# blocks is edited; generated ones can't.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
